1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,544
Teacher midterm practice, question 31.

2
00:00:04,164 --> 00:00:08,639
True or false: F C C and B C C metals are generally ductile because

3
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:12,673
they have enough good slip systems, whereas H C P metals are

4
00:00:12,673 --> 00:00:17,148
generally more brittle, with fewer independent slip systems.

5
00:00:18,849 --> 00:00:23,211
A metal needs enough independent slip systems to change its shape.

6
00:00:23,211 --> 00:00:26,438
F C C has twelve, and B C C twelve or more.

7
00:00:27,058 --> 00:00:30,141
H C P has only a few, on its basal plane, so at

8
00:00:30,141 --> 00:00:33,111
room temperature it is generally less ductile.

9
00:00:34,711 --> 00:00:36,427
So the answer is A: true.

10
00:00:37,247 --> 00:00:40,911
Brittle here means comparatively less ductile, not glass brittle.
